---
import SectionHeading from "../shared/SectionHeading.astro";
import { fourCapabilities } from "../../data/evercompass";
---

<section class="border-t border-slate-100 bg-white">
  <div class="mx-auto max-w-5xl px-6 py-20 md:py-28">
    <SectionHeading
      eyebrow="What EverCompass Draws On"
      headline="Four capabilities. One decision."
      subhead="Together, they cover most of where a growth constraint tends to show up — positioning, experience, communication, and measurement."
    />
    <p class="mt-8 max-w-3xl text-lg text-slate-600">
      Depending on what the diagnosis finds, the fix might be strategic,
      experiential, message-driven, or systems-based — often more than one. These
      aren't services to choose from. They're the four capabilities EverCompass
      has to work with, and it decides which ones a given situation actually
      needs. EverCompass determines the priorities. Marketing Strategy is one of
      the four capabilities it calls on — specifically when the priority itself
      is strategic, like positioning or focus — not a competing source of
      prioritization.
    </p>
    <ul class="mt-12 grid gap-6 sm:grid-cols-2">
      {
        fourCapabilities.map((cap) => (
          <li class="rounded-xl border border-slate-200 bg-stone-50 p-6">
            <h3 class="font-serif text-xl font-semibold text-slate-900">
              {cap.name}
            </h3>
            <p class="mt-2 text-slate-600">{cap.body}</p>
          </li>
        ))
      }
    </ul>
  </div>
</section>
